{\cite[Theorem 1.3]{M23}} \label{T1.3}Let $m,n$, and $r$ be nonnegative integers such that $0\leq r<m$. We have 
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] $\displaystyle a_{r,m}(n)=\sum_{j=0}^\infty (mj+r)p(n-mj-r)$; 
\item[(ii)] $\displaystyle s_m(n)= \sum_{j=0}^\infty jp(n-mj)$.
\end{itemize}

